lunduke-paint (0.9-10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The main window fits a 1280x768 screen with a panel. The Layers,
    History, and Colors column scrolls, and those lists can shrink, so the
    wells, pattern strip, and status bar stay on screen.
  * New pictures follow the umask. Saving over an existing file keeps its
    permission bits and, where the system allows, its owner and group.
  * Flatten and keep .ora names the companion file, asks before replacing
    one that is not this picture, and updates that file on later saves.
  * Undo keeps the newest step, says when older steps are dropped, and the
    history list names the oldest state it can actually restore.
  * A flat save warns once for each document and target. Enter confirms
    New Image, Canvas Size, Scale, and the other dialogs. Save Image shows
    JPEG quality only when the file that will be written is a JPEG.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 23:20:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.9-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Foreground and background wells, and the swap and reset controls, have
    tooltips and accessible names. The tool rail stays 82 px and does not
    grow text labels.
  * A typed file extension wins over the Save As filter. The filter adds an
    extension only when the name has none. An unknown extension asks before
    anything is written. Save and Save As share that rule.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:45:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.9-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The tool rail is back to the classic MacPaint width from 0.5-4 (82 px).
    Foreground and background wells, swap and reset, the extra tool
    buttons, and the line, brush, and spray pickers sit in that column.
    The pattern strip, colours dock, and F12 are unchanged.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 20:15:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.9-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Foreground and background wells sit on the tool rail, with swap and
    reset. A palette swatch sets the foreground on left-click and the
    background on right-click; editing a swatch is a double-click.
  * Picker, magic wand, ellipse select, curve, and polyline have toolbox
    buttons. The highlighted button follows the active tool.
  * Patterns paint the brush, the fill bucket, and filled-shape interiors.
    Pencil strokes and shape outlines stay solid. Zoom to Fit uses the
    largest ratio that fits.
  * Zoomed-out compositing samples the visible screen and caches it. Blur is
    a separable box over the selection or the layer. Undo stores changed
    patches and drops the oldest steps past 256 MB.
  * The tool rail keeps square buttons and a full-width width picker. Menu
    mnemonics and the shortcut list cover the keys the app uses. Layer
    opacity and blend are on the layers panel.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:30:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.9-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A floating selection from paste, move, drag-in, transform, nudge, or a
    margin placement is unsaved work: it is undoable, and crash recovery
    stores it. A lasso or ellipse mask stays with scale, rotate, flip, nudge,
    crop, copy, cut, paste, copy-merged, and paste-into-new.
  * Save on close waits for a file name. Text that paints nothing no longer
    blocks Save. The tool rail scrolls instead of clipping, the canvas cursor
    follows the tool, and Escape cancels a resting float.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.9-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * An in-progress shape, an open text box, pasted text, or a floating
    selection is stamped onto its own layer, kept, or asked about. Tool
    changes, undo, open, tabs, quit, layer edits, save, paste, and recovery
    no longer drop that work or put it on the wrong layer.
  * Shape options follow the fill-mode key. Transparent move is one setting.
    Brush tips do not move the line-width mark. Fill and the wand run the
    similarity number on their own spin.
  * A failed recovery open keeps the file. The package build runs the GUI
    tests under Xvfb when DISPLAY is unset (Build-Depends: xvfb, xauth) and
    fails if those tests cannot get a display.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:45:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.9-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stroke width follows the left-rail picker for lines, shapes, and the
    eraser. A solid canvas no longer autocrops to a single pixel.
  * An open polygon, polyline, curve, or text box stays with its tab, shows
    the dirty mark, and is stamped only when the user saves or switches away.
    Quit Cancel leaves the edit in place.
  * Each dirty tab keeps its own crash-recovery file, including committed
    pixels and an open text box. Saving one tab no longer deletes the others.
  * Undo of a selection move restores the selection. A locked layer blocks
    the next action instead of dropping a floating selection.
  * Tool options (font, similarity, transparent move, antialias, corner
    radius) sit in the left rail. Status text is visible again, and save
    errors include the operating-system reason. Shortcut help matches the keys.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 07:30:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.9-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Undo trim no longer treats a dropped baseline as the saved file.
    Masked selections punch, stamp, and delete only covered pixels.
  * Save, print, quit, and close stamp an open text box. A failed float
    stamp aborts the save and keeps the recovery file. Saves write an
    exclusive temporary file, fsync, and rename, and refuse a final symlink.
  * Save As replaces the extension on the file name only. OpenRaster reads
    reject oversized entries, and non-isolated groups composite against the
    backdrop. Flood fill and merge down no longer pump the main loop.
  * Crash recovery encodes without GdkPixbuf, skips a live effect preview,
    and uses a private 0700 directory. Multi-frame GIFs warn on open.
    Recent-file labels do not treat underscore as a mnemonic.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.9-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Selection move composites the visible rect once and blends the float
    in bulk. Shape previews invalidate the previous outline and restore
    only that rectangle.
  * Hand, space, and middle-button pan use screen coordinates. Ctrl+wheel
    zoom keeps the point under the cursor after scrolling.
  * Crash recovery no longer commits a floating selection. Autosave encodes
    a snapshot on a worker and skips mergedimage.png on a large canvas
    until the document has been idle.
  * Selection lift, delete, fill, and commit convert canvas space to the
    source layer. Changing the active layer commits the float there.
  * OpenRaster groups composite with group opacity, visibility, and blend,
    including a root stack offset. Copy Merged keeps layers under a cut.
  * Marching ants cache one path. Selection drag updates the status bar
    without rebuilding the layers and history panels.
  * Merge Down blends onto the lower layer and bakes a backdrop only when
    that layer is non-Normal and partially transparent.
  * Zoomed-in redraw uses the same nearest-neighbor scale as zoom-out.
    Flood fill and the magic wand use a scanline fill and a tight mask.
    Box blur is premultiplied. Spraycan steps along the stroke. Paint
    inside a selection clips the latest stamp. Scale, rotate, and canvas
    size store one pre-image. The checkerboard is a repeated pattern.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 06:30:00 -0500

